WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:10.062
"Is your air on?" asks Josh.

2
00:00:10.063 --> 00:00:15.853
"Is your air on?" asks Anne. "Okay, let's go!"

3
00:00:15.854 --> 00:00:22.459
Today Josh and Anne are taking us on a scuba-diving adventure near the Similan Islands in Thailand.

4
00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:29.892
The water here is so clear that we can see things thirty meters away, and that's pretty far for being underwater!

5
00:00:29.893 --> 00:00:35.498
Whenever people go scuba diving, they swim in a group for safety, so we had better stay together!

6
00:00:35.499 --> 00:00:40.193
There are hundreds of great places to scuba dive in the world, and each of them is different.

7
00:00:40.194 --> 00:00:46.764
Some places are very cold, or are filled with seaweed, or have only very small animals.

8
00:00:46.765 --> 00:00:55.004
The Similan Islands, however, are great because the water is 28 degrees Celsius and crystal clear, and there are lots of big fish.

9
00:00:55.005 --> 00:01:00.107
In fact, look over there! Josh has found a moray eel hiding in the rocks.

10
00:01:00.108 --> 00:01:05.032
Don't worry; it is more frightened of us than we are of it.

11
00:01:05.033 --> 00:01:06.730
Look at its sharp teeth!

12
00:01:06.731 --> 00:01:11.685
It has two sets of jaws to pull its prey in, so keep your hands far away!

13
00:01:11.686 --> 00:01:16.399
Eels aren't very friendly creatures, as you can tell, and they mostly live alone.

14
00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.306
So we probably won't see another eel for quite a while.

15
00:01:20.307 --> 00:01:23.847
Did you know that there are hundreds of plants that live underwater?

16
00:01:23.848 --> 00:01:25.926
Thailand has many kinds.

17
00:01:25.927 --> 00:01:32.438
One plantlike creature is called coral, and there are two kinds: hard coral and soft coral.

18
00:01:32.439 --> 00:01:37.624
A coral is built from live cells that stack on top of each other in layers.

19
00:01:37.625 --> 00:01:45.074
When the outer layer gets old, a new layer of cells forms around it so the plant grows taller or wider.

20
00:01:45.075 --> 00:01:51.418
Like their names suggest, hard coral is stiff, while soft coral is able to sway with the ocean current.

21
00:01:51.419 --> 00:01:54.691
Both soft and hard coral grow very slowly.

22
00:01:54.692 --> 00:02:01.754
Look, this fan coral grows about one centimeter each year, so Anne is careful not to touch it as she swims by.

23
00:02:01.755 --> 00:02:08.922
Touching a coral can kill it, and sometimes it can hurt us too so we stay far away.

24
00:02:08.923 --> 00:02:13.770
Look, down at the bottom—there's a whale shark, the biggest fish in the world!

25
00:02:13.771 --> 00:02:19.271
Anne is trying to get her picture taken with it, but don't worry, this shark won't bite.

26
00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:25.129
Whale sharks only eat small animals and tiny plants that float in the water called plankton.

27
00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:29.982
Still, we're careful not to disturb the shark since this is its home.

28
00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:35.117
Josh is checking his pressure gauges, and signals to Anne that he is almost out of air.

29
00:02:35.118 --> 00:02:40.337
Men use up air faster than women because their lungs are bigger and because they have more muscle,

30
00:02:40.338 --> 00:02:45.164
but I think we have enough time to look at just a couple more creatures.

31
00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:49.717
Oh no, Anne is giving the danger signal! She found a sea snake.

32
00:02:49.718 --> 00:02:56.731
This underwater creature may be tiny, but its venom is twenty times more poisonous than any snake on land!

33
00:02:56.732 --> 00:03:01.703
It eats mostly small fish by paralyzing them first with one quick bite.

34
00:03:01.704 --> 00:03:04.613
It takes less than a second for its venom to work.

35
00:03:04.614 --> 00:03:08.387
The sea snake seems to be a little hungry, so we'll move on.

36
00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:11.603
Here is Josh's favorite animal, the cuttlefish.

37
00:03:11.604 --> 00:03:17.386
Many people eat cuttlefish thinking it is an ordinary squid, but it is really an amazing animal.

38
00:03:17.387 --> 00:03:22.634
Watch carefully. The mother cuttlefish is trying to protect its baby by distracting us.

39
00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:26.773
See how its skin is changing colors so that we can see it better?

40
00:03:26.774 --> 00:03:31.761
Cuttlefish can change the color and texture of their skin to match anything around them.

41
00:03:31.762 --> 00:03:37.785
For example, if there is a field of black rocks nearby, their skin will turn bumpy and black.

42
00:03:37.786 --> 00:03:42.348
If they swim by green seaweed, they will turn smooth and green.

43
00:03:42.349 --> 00:03:47.748
If you put down a purple polka-dot blanket, their skin will have polka dots!

44
00:03:47.749 --> 00:03:50.167
It looks like Josh is low on air.

45
00:03:50.168 --> 00:03:54.620
It's time to return to our own world above-water, but don't be disappointed.

46
00:03:54.621 --> 00:03:58.389
There will always be another adventure!
